{
  "method": "For a horizontal soffit, angular elevation above the eye on its front at a given image column divided by elevation at its rear wall contact equals the ratio of their horizontal distances. In the same camera, depth out of wall = perpendicular distance to wall * (1 - (rear chart z - eye)/(front chart z - eye)). This cancels station drift, the arbitrary trial projection plane and common vertical scale. Calibrated camera height 2.32 m, distances to west wall 5.938 and 5.505 m. Front edges at upper camera distances checked in both directions. The two outer reads stop just clear of the projecting narrow separator; remaining 8–16 cm across the facet can change apparent depth by a few cm.",
